Chapter: Entry Point
  cites Codex chapter Opening (codex-opening)

 Two definitions named `opening` in one compilation unit collide, so a program
 that supplies its OWN entry point could not bundle Chapter: Opening at all,
 and therefore could not call the compiler's phases. This chapter holds the
 entry point and nothing else, which leaves that chapter bundlable. The body
 is `codex-opening`, one chapter over, unchanged.

Section: Entry Point

  opening : [Console, FileSystem, Device.Block] Nothing = codex-opening

